>
  <h1>Repositories</h1>
  <p>
    Listed here when a public repository shows a problem, a stack, engineering decisions, and tests
    or CI.
  </p>

  <h2>Commerce Operations Console</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/chrisuzor/commerce-ops-console">github.com/chrisuzor/commerce-ops-console</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    It demonstrates investigation of failed commerce orders. Events from payment, fulfillment, and
    notification systems are stored as an append-only history. Idempotency keys collapse duplicate
    deliveries, and a deterministic summary is built only from stored events. The stack is Go,
    GraphQL, PostgreSQL, React, and TypeScript. Go tests, <code>go vet</code>, and the React lint,
    test, and build run in CI.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is a portfolio sample, not a hosted order processor, and it is not the Mews permission-aware
    investigation workflow.
  </p>
</Base>
